7. Mandatory profile re-review when a fighter changes

This requirement is important:

Whenever a fighter’s character definition changes, their Discover profile must be explicitly rechecked.

Do not satisfy this with only a comment saying “remember to review it.” Add an automated guard so the repository tells us when the review is stale.

Implement a test-time source-review fingerprint.

Recommended approach:

1. Keep fighter profile metadata in a file separate from js/data/characters/<id>.js.
2. For every fighter profile, store a reviewedSourceHash representing the associated js/data/characters/<id>.js source at the time its difficulty/play-style profile was reviewed.
3. Add a Node test that:
    * reads the character source file as UTF-8,
    * normalizes line endings to \n,
    * calculates a SHA-256 digest,
    * compares it with that profile’s reviewedSourceHash.
4. If the fighter source changes, the test must fail with an explicit message similar to:
    #0001 changed since its Discover profile was reviewed. Recheck its difficulty and play-style description, then update reviewedSourceHash.

This hash is a maintenance/review guard only. It is not gameplay behavior.

When implementing this feature, review both current fighters against their current definitions and then generate/store their current hashes.

This intentionally means a change to the fighter definition requires somebody to look at the profile again before tests pass.

Also add coverage so a newly playable fighter cannot ship without:

* a valid 1–5 difficulty,
* a play-style description key,
* a current review hash.

Do not create a self-referential hash by storing the hash inside the character source file itself.

